Ha! Code rot — digital decomposition. 😂

Software has a half-life, even when nobody touches it.

Dependencies decay, interfaces change, assumptions expire, and yesterday’s elegant solution becomes tomorrow’s archaeological dig.

But here’s the interesting distinction: sometimes the code hasn’t rotted at all. The world around it has.

It’s evolutionary mismatch in software.

And there’s a deeper version: semantic rot — when the instructions still execute perfectly, but the original meaning, purpose, or context has disappeared.

The machine remembers how. Nobody remembers why.

Digital fossils. 🦴